thread:
Laura Chen: Quick heads-up — we're scheduling the v1 models endpoint deprecation for next Wed (rollout window 03:00-07:00 UTC). Need to confirm a couple of SDK/docs edge cases and a rollback checklist. Tagging docs + SDK folks.
Samir Patel: Thanks. main questions: what happens to long-running streaming clients when we swap model variants? do we force-close streams or proxy? :thinking_face:
Kevin O'Malley: We shouldn't force-close if avoidable. Suggest proxy to compatible v2 variant and return a deprecation header so clients can retry gracefully.
Maria Gomez: For migration guide: I have a draft that replaces the old `models` endpoint example with `model-versions` usage. Also highlight embedding model swaps. Will push a snippet.
Laura Chen: @Samir good call — need explicit behavior in the SDK change log. Add a snippet showing reconnect pattern. Also: verify that existing SDKs return a clear error code for requests that relied on v1-only parameters.
Samir Patel: I'll open an SDK PR to surface `DEPRECATED_MODEL_ENDPOINT` error code and add a `reconnect()` helper for streaming. Planning tests for: 1) running stream during model swap 2) stream resume token correctness. ETA EOD Tue.
Kevin O'Malley: Docs action items: update REST examples, update python/ts SDK snippets, and add a small migration table mapping v1 param -> v2 param. I added a note about token cost differences in the migration doc — people need to check usage.
Maria Gomez: Draft PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4723 — contains new examples and a fallback strategy section. Please review.
docs-bot: Automated check — PR 4723: lint OK, broken-links scan: 1 warning (old sdk link), includes `TODO: verify streaming behavior`.
Laura Chen: Kevin/Maria — can you sync on the streaming code snippet? We should include both server-side and client-side minimal examples.
Kevin O'Malley: Pushed a short client-side snippet to the PR. Example (JS):
```js
// old v1
const res = await client.post('/v1/models/generate', { prompt });

// new v2
const res = await client.post('/v2/model-versions/generate', { model: 'gpt-rlhf-v2', prompt });
```
Suggest adding a reconnect skeleton:
```js
async function streamWithReconnect(url, opts) {
  let cursor = null;
  while(true) {
    const stream = await openStream(url, { cursor, ...opts });
    for await (const chunk of stream) {
      // process chunk
      cursor = chunk.cursor || cursor;
    }
    if (!shouldRetry()) break;
  }
}
```
Samir Patel: That skeleton helps. For Python snippet I'll mirror that but use an async generator and an explicit resume token.
Maria Gomez: One more: need to clarify model-swap fallback order in docs. Our policy is: 1) same family quantized variant 2) same family float16 3) any compatible family that supports requested features (streaming, functions). I'll add a small table.
Laura Chen: Also decide on communication plan: embedded in deprecation notice email, console banner, and SDK change logs. Coordinate with growth for email.
Kevin O'Malley: I will draft the console banner copy: "Heads-up: v1 models endpoint will be retired on YYYY-MM-DD. Update to v2 to avoid service interruptions." Short + link to migration guide.
Samir Patel: Tests: I'll add an integration test that simulates a model swap mid-stream and asserts resume token semantics. Will include a flaky-handling note.
Maria Gomez: One edge case: customers using custom routing rules (region pinning) — we need to document that fallback may change region unless they pin the model version. I'll add an FAQ entry.
Laura Chen: Thanks everyone. Owners: SDK PR -> @Samir, Docs PR reviews + snippets -> @Maria and @Kevin, Communication copy -> @Kevin. I'll post a short deprecation notice once PRs merged. Marking this thread as the coordination point.
Kevin O'Malley: Acknowledged. :thumbsup:
Laura Chen: Marking resolved for now — ping me if anything blocks tomorrow.
